      "response": {
        "category": "correctness",
        "consequence": "The `queued` value is stale for every assignment source. It grows more wrong the longer the worker or web process runs. Anything that reads `queued` for ordering, staleness or cycle detection will get wrong results.",
        "evidence_refs": [
          "source:new:src/sentry/integrations/services/assignment_source.py@sha256:885ab5f3b8ef5398cf84e90112d9352978908c663d9034ef89e7ed4eccfdfa0e"
        ],
        "explanation": "`queued: datetime = timezone.now()` is a dataclass default, so `timezone.now()` runs once when the module is imported. Every `AssignmentSource` built through `from_integration` gets that same fixed timestamp, which is the process start time, not the time the assignment was queued. `to_dict` then sends this wrong value to the task through `asdict`. The fix is `field(default_factory=timezone.now)`. This also stops the datetime from being frozen into the class definition.",
        "lines": {
          "end_line": 18,
          "start_line": 18
        },
